# Jimmy's ruling, 12 November: `ValueOf: forall (r: k). k`, the value of a promoted case
# named as a type. Its `k` is the kind of a payload-free choice; `Text` is a type, no case
# of any choice, so `ValueOf<<Text>>` is a kind error.
# Expected diagnostic derived by hand. Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting
# branch; subject to change.
Valued: fn Nat -> Text
fn Valued n = ValueOf<<Text>>
